Sprint 35: the round-trip law harness (invariant 10).

Empty by design.  `make test-fletch-roundtrip` hard-errors naming the
sprint rather than passing vacuously, because a harness that reports
green over zero cases is worse than one that refuses to run: the first
is mistaken for coverage.

The law: a recorded session emitted as Fletch, re-parsed and re-emitted,
must produce byte-identical text.  Sprint 35 supplies the recorder that
makes a case writable at all.
